{"seq":1,"type":"message_received","time":"2026-10-11T12:00:43.310774Z","message":{"actor":"human","parts":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a bounded memory exercise in an empty scratch workspace. Do not use filesystem or command tools. Analyze the supplied case, explain the decision briefly, then call micro_handoff exactly once with the important facts and reasons. After the tool returns, finish this turn without another tool call. Case one: Our project is Cedar Lantern, release code CL-721. We rejected automatic deletion of imported notes because the support team needs the originals when customers report mistakes. The replacement design keeps source notes in an archive and stores the accepted summary separately. Morgan owns the archive review, scheduled for October 18. Acceptance requires preserving a source identifier with each summary. The unresolved question is whether attachments belong in the same archive or a separate one; do not claim that has been decided. The default retention is thirty days. A failed summarization must leave the original note available. The initial approach coupled cleanup to request arrival, so an unrelated request could delete unreviewed work. We moved cleanup to an explicit completed-review boundary instead. Explain why the latter boundary matters, and preserve these facts in your checkpoint."}]}}
{"seq":2,"type":"request_sent","time":"2026-10-11T12:00:43.311193Z","request":{"to":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"},"startup_tools":[{"name":"read_file","description":"Read text with one-based inclusive start_line/end_line. Optional max_bytes bounds the read; job reports cap inline output and preserve the full result on disk.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"},"max_bytes":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"list_directory","description":"List immediate entries, sorted by name; directories end with /.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"search_files","description":"Search files recursively using a regular expression. context_lines defaults to zero. Output uses grep path:line:text and path-line-context with merged windows.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"pattern":{"type":"string"},"context_lines":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","pattern"]}},{"name":"write_file","description":"Write text, creating parent directories. Existing files require overwrite:true unless append:true. Append preserves existing content.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"},"overwrite":{"type":"boolean"},"append":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","content"]}},{"name":"edit_file","description":"Replace one exact, unique old_text anchor with new_text. Zero or multiple matches refuse without changing the file; read and provide a more specific anchor.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"old_text":{"type":"string"},"new_text":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","old_text","new_text"]}},{"name":"run_command","description":"Start a fresh /bin/sh in a PTY. cwd applies only to this call, relative to the workspace. Merged output and exit_code stay on disk; a running report is a handle, not cancellation. ai_callback_delay is seconds (default 3); pattern matches unseen output; max_output_bytes defaults to 16384.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string"},"cwd":{"type":"string"},"ai_callback_delay":{"type":"number","description":"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline"},"ai_callback_pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Regex on unseen output"},"max_output_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"Inline output byte cap, default 16384"}},"required":["command"]}},{"name":"wait_for_job","description":"Wait for a job, including a finished job. Return only unseen output; waiting does not stop execution.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"handle":{"type":"integer"},"ai_callback_delay":{"type":"number","description":"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline"},"ai_callback_pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Regex on unseen output"},"max_output_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"Inline output byte cap, default 16384"}},"required":["handle"]}},{"name":"send_input","description":"Send a line of input to a running PTY job, then wait. A missing trailing newline is added.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"handle":{"type":"integer"},"input":{"type":"string"},"ai_callback_delay":{"type":"number","description":"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline"},"ai_callback_pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Regex on unseen output"},"max_output_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"Inline output byte cap, default 16384"}},"required":["handle","input"]}},{"name":"kill_job","description":"Kill a job's process group. Go-only work is marked killed but its goroutine cannot be stopped.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"handle":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["handle"]}},{"name":"tool_limits","description":"Set one-shot wait/output limits for the very next call, whichever tool it is. That call reports consumption; explicit call arguments override these limits.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ai_callback_delay":{"type":"number","description":"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline"},"ai_callback_pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Regex on unseen output"},"max_output_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"Inline output byte cap, default 16384"}},"required":[]}},{"name":"micro_handoff","description":"Checkpoint at a completed micro-goal. Write text with what succeeded, what failed, source locations and next steps. Removes all tool traffic but preserves conversation and this note.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"}},"required":["text"]}},{"name":"keep_tool_results","description":"Keep the previous batch of tool results instead of automatic stubbing on supported models. Does not keep results of tools called alongside this call.","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}}]}}
{"seq":3,"type":"response_ended","time":"2026-10-11T12:00:46.723684Z","response":{"parts":[{"artifact_id":1,"type":"opaque","from":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"},"data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"artifact_id":2,"type":"text","text":"The explicit completed-review boundary matters because deletion should depend on a finished review, not on unrelated traffic. Under the old design, any request could trigger cleanup and remove notes nobody had reviewed yet. Support could then lose the originals they need when customers report mistakes. Tying cleanup to a completed review keeps originals available until that review is done."},{"artifact_id":3,"type":"tool_call","from":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"},"call_id":"toolu_01S5f9irGhJA2dE2uqdSme2T","name":"micro_handoff","args":{"text":"Checkpoint for Cedar Lantern (release CL-721):\n- Decision: rejected automatic deletion of imported notes. Support needs originals when customers report mistakes.\n- Replacement design: source notes stay in an archive; the accepted summary is stored separately.\n- Acceptance requirement: each summary must preserve a source identifier.\n- Owner and date: Morgan owns the archive review, scheduled for October 18.\n- Open question (not decided): whether attachments belong in the same archive or a separate one.\n- Default retention: thirty days.\n- Failure rule: a failed summarization must leave the original note available.\n- Cleanup change: the initial design tied cleanup to request arrival, so an unrelated request could delete unreviewed work. Cleanup now runs at an explicit completed-review boundary instead.\n- Rationale for boundary: deletion waits for a finished review, so originals stay available until review is complete."}}],"usage":{"input":2628,"cache_write":0,"cache_read":0,"output":652},"from":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"}}}
