{"seq":6,"type":"micro_handoff","time":"2026-10-11T12:00:46.726647Z","handoff":{"text":"Checkpoint for Cedar Lantern (release CL-721):\n- Decision: rejected automatic deletion of imported notes. Support needs originals when customers report mistakes.\n- Replacement design: source notes stay in an archive; the accepted summary is stored separately.\n- Acceptance requirement: each summary must preserve a source identifier.\n- Owner and date: Morgan owns the archive review, scheduled for October 18.\n- Open question (not decided): whether attachments belong in the same archive or a separate one.\n- Default retention: thirty days.\n- Failure rule: a failed summarization must leave the original note available.\n- Cleanup change: the initial design tied cleanup to request arrival, so an unrelated request could delete unreviewed work. Cleanup now runs at an explicit completed-review boundary instead.\n- Rationale for boundary: deletion waits for a finished review, so originals stay available until review is complete."}}
