{"seq":20,"type":"band_populated","time":"2026-10-11T12:01:00.76833Z","populated":{"band":5,"file":{"date":"2026-10-11","num":2},"text":"I designed the archive lifecycle as follows. Originals stay in the archive. Accepted summaries are stored separately, tagged with a source identifier. If summarization fails, the original stays available. Cleanup runs only after a completed review, never because of an unrelated request. Two items are still open. First, if the 30-day retention expires before the October 18 review finishes, I have not yet decided whether the original is deleted or held. My current reading is that originals remain available until the review is done, but the spec does not say so explicitly, so it needs to be written down. Second, attachments are undecided: they could share the notes archive or get their own. That choice affects retention and review scope, so it should be settled before October 18. I offered to draft a decision record for either item, and that offer is pending.\n\nCase two is the Harbor Finch deployment rehearsal (diagnostic tag HF-934), owned by Priya and scheduled for October 21. Decided: I rejected automatic retry of a database migration after a timeout, because the remote operation may already have committed. The procedure reads the migration ledger before deciding whether any retry is safe. The operator must record the exact migration identifier and the measured error, not a guess about success. The rollback package must remain available for seven days after deployment. New evidence: last week a log line said the worker had stopped, but the child process was still alive and holding the port. Log messages are not proof of process state, so the rehearsal now checks child lifetime directly. Unresolved: whether the migration ledger lives alongside application data or in a separate control database. Next steps: confirm the ledger location before the October 21 rehearsal, and verify that the child-lifetime check is in the rehearsal procedure.","thru":{"date":"2026-10-11","num":2},"source":"compression"}}
