{"seq":23,"type":"band_populated","time":"2026-10-11T12:01:06.671859Z","populated":{"band":4,"file":{"date":"2026-10-11","num":1},"text":"I am working on Cedar Lantern (release CL-721). I rejected automatic deletion of imported notes because support needs originals when customers report mistakes. Design: originals stay in an archive; accepted summaries are stored separately, each tagged with its source identifier; if summarization fails, the original stays available. Default retention is 30 days. Cleanup runs only after a completed review, never because of an unrelated request, since cleanup tied to request arrival could delete unreviewed work. Morgan owns archive review, scheduled October 18.\n\nOpen for Cedar Lantern: (1) If the 30-day retention expires before the October 18 review finishes, I have not decided whether the original is deleted or held. My reading is that originals stay available until review is done, but the spec doesn't say so; this needs to be written down. (2) Attachments: same archive or a separate one is undecided. It affects retention and review scope and should be settled before October 18. I offered to draft a decision record for either item; that offer is pending.\n\nCase two: Harbor Finch deployment rehearsal (diagnostic tag HF-934), owned by Priya, scheduled October 21. Decided: I rejected automatic retry of a database migration after a timeout, because the remote operation may already have committed. The procedure reads the migration ledger before deciding whether a retry is safe. The operator records the exact migration identifier and the measured error, not a guess about success. The rollback package stays available for seven days after deployment. New evidence: a log line said the worker had stopped, but the child process was still alive holding the port. Log messages are not proof of process state, so the rehearsal checks child lifetime directly.\n\nUnresolved: whether the migration ledger lives with application data or in a separate control database. Next steps: confirm the ledger location before the October 21 rehearsal, and verify the child-lifetime check is in the rehearsal procedure.","thru":{"date":"2026-10-11","num":2},"source":"compression"}}
