{"seq":25,"type":"response_ended","time":"2026-10-11T12:01:10.443523Z","response":{"parts":[{"artifact_id":11,"type":"opaque","from":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"},"data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"artifact_id":12,"type":"text","text":"Here's where things stand.\n\n**Cedar Lantern (CL-721): open items**\n1. **Retention past 30 days.** Not yet decided whether an original is deleted or held if review isn't finished when retention expires. Your reading (originals stay available until review completes) isn't in the spec yet, so it needs a written decision.\n2. **Attachments.** Same archive or a separate one is undecided. This affects retention and review scope, so settle it before **October 18** (Morgan's archive review).\n\n**Harbor Finch rehearsal (HF-934, Priya, October 21)**\n- **Ledger location.** Unresolved: application data or a separate control database. Confirm before the rehearsal.\n- **Child-lifetime check.** Confirm it's in the procedure. The \"worker stopped\" log line isn't evidence, so the check must verify the child process directly, since the child was still holding the port.\n\nDo you want me to draft decision records for the Cedar Lantern retention question and the attachments question, and a checklist for the Harbor Finch procedure covering the ledger location and child-lifetime check? Tell me where to save them."}],"usage":{"input":2871,"cache_write":0,"cache_read":0,"output":682},"from":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"}}}
