{"seq":28,"type":"response_ended","time":"2026-10-11T12:01:15.557448Z","response":{"parts":[{"artifact_id":13,"type":"opaque","from":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"},"data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"artifact_id":14,"type":"text","text":"**Cedar Lantern (release CL-721)**\n- **Owner:** Morgan, archive review, scheduled **October 18**.\n- **Design:** Originals stay in an archive. Accepted summaries are stored separately, each tagged with its source identifier. If summarization fails, the original stays available. Default retention is 30 days.\n- **Rejected:**\n  - *Automatic deletion of imported notes.* Support needs originals when customers report mistakes.\n  - *Cleanup triggered by request arrival.* It could delete unreviewed work. Cleanup runs only after a completed review.\n\n**Harbor Finch deployment rehearsal (diagnostic tag HF-934)**\n- **Owner:** Priya, rehearsal scheduled **October 21**.\n- **Decided:** The operator reads the migration ledger before deciding whether a retry is safe. The operator records the exact migration identifier and the measured error. The rollback package stays available for seven days after deployment.\n- **Rejected:**\n  - *Automatic retry of a database migration after a timeout.* The remote operation may already have committed.\n  - *Treating a log line as proof of process state.* A \"worker stopped\" line didn't match reality: the child process was still alive holding the port. The rehearsal checks child lifetime directly.\n\n**The two unresolved questions (Cedar Lantern)**\n1. **Retention past 30 days:** If retention expires before the October 18 review finishes, it's undecided whether the original is deleted or held. Your reading (stay available until review is done) is not in the spec yet and has not been decided.\n2. **Attachments:** Same archive or a separate one is undecided. This affects retention and review scope and should be settled before October 18.\n\n**Also open (Harbor Finch):** Whether the migration ledger lives with application data or in a separate control database. This is unresolved and must be confirmed before October 21. Verifying that the child-lifetime check is in the procedure is a pending next step, not a decided item."}],"usage":{"input":3622,"cache_write":0,"cache_read":0,"output":1169},"from":{"vendor":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","surface":"messages"}}}
